# Arc Foundry — Showcase

The finished game ships a showcase: the store-page presentation a player reads before
deciding to play. It is a `showcase/` directory at the root of this repository, committed
with the rest of the project, holding a description of the game and a short carousel of
captured media. This file defines its contents.

## Layout

Every file of the showcase sits directly in `showcase/`, with no subdirectories:

- `showcase/showcase.md`, the description.
- `showcase/showcase.toml`, the carousel.
- The media files the carousel and the description name.

## The description

`showcase/showcase.md` is Markdown written for a player: what Arc Foundry is, how a yard
is walled into a maze out of rolls the player did not pick, and what climbing the quality
ladder and assembling a combination tower offer. Three to five short paragraphs. It is
strictly about playing the game; implementation, architecture, and tooling stay out of
it. It may embed images that sit beside it, referenced by bare relative path (for example
`![The yard](yard.png)`); every image it embeds is a `.png` in `showcase/`.

## The carousel

`showcase/showcase.toml` lists the media in the order they are presented, one `[[media]]`
table per entry:

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
```toml
[[media]]
file = "wave.webm"
name = "A wave crawling the maze under fire"

[[media]]
file = "title.png"
name = "The title screen"
```
{{else}}
```toml
[[media]]
file = "wave.json.gz"
name = "A wave crawling the maze under fire"

[[media]]
file = "title.png"
name = "The title screen"
```
{{/if}}

- `file` names a file directly in `showcase/`, with no path separators. Every file the
  carousel names exists there, and each stays under 25 MiB.
- `name` is a caption of a few words.
- The carousel holds two to four entries. The first entry leads, so it carries the
  strongest view of live play.

## Media

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The file extension states what an entry is:

| Extension | Media |
| --- | --- |
| `.png` | A screenshot of the running game. |
| `.webm` | A video clip of the running game, a few seconds long. |

Screenshots carry most of the carousel. Where motion is worth showing, such as a wave
walking a long maze while the towers fire on it, a short `.webm` clip carries it; how
screenshots and clips are captured is the build's own business.
{{else}}
The file extension states what an entry is:

| Extension | Media |
| --- | --- |
| `.png` | A screenshot of the running game. |
| `.json.gz` | A replay: a gzipped recording of the game's own drawing, made with the engine's recorder. |
| `.webm` | A video clip. |

Anything in motion is captured as a replay rather than a video.

## Capturing a replay

A replay is a gzipped JSON recording made with the engine's recorder, which the engine
documents in `engine/recording.md` at the root of this repository. Each replay holds a
few seconds of live play, such as a wave crossing the maze while the towers fire on it,
rather than a menu. How screenshots and replays are captured is the build's own business.
{{/if}}
